B) Use feature flags or similar mechanisms to control which prompt/model variant is
   active per environment or per rollout stage, rather than relying on hand-edited
   config with no record of what's currently live where.
C) Store production secrets directly in the same repository as the versioned prompt
   fragments, since keeping everything in one place simplifies configuration tracking.
D) Rely on each engineer's personal recollection of the last production change, since
   documentation inevitably goes stale and isn't worth the maintenance overhead.
E) Skip having any rollback plan for configuration changes, since a well-tested change
   should never need to be rolled back in practice.

