   basis.
B) Manually pre-judging every request's difficulty and disabling thinking uniformly for
   an entire category removes exactly the benefit adaptive thinking is meant to
   provide — letting the model decide, per request, whether a given input (even
   within a generally "simple" category) actually warrants deeper reasoning, rather
   than a blanket human judgment applied to the whole category regardless of
   per-input variation.
C) Adaptive thinking cannot be used selectively at all; it must be either fully enabled
   or fully disabled for an entire application, with no per-request nuance possible.
D) The `effort` parameter has no relationship to adaptive thinking and instead governs
   an unrelated aspect of the request, such as `max_tokens`.

