   mechanism for any reference content regardless of whether it's live external data
   or static packaged knowledge.
B) The live pricing data fits an MCP resource (content read from an actual external
   system, potentially changing between reads), while the static style guide fits a
   Skill (packaged procedural/reference knowledge with no external system behind it,
   loaded on demand) — the source of the content (a live external system versus
   self-contained packaged material) is what distinguishes the right mechanism, not
   how "important" either piece of content is.
C) Both should be modeled identically as MCP resources, since resources are the only
   mechanism MCP defines for exposing any reference content whatsoever.
D) The distinction between a resource and a Skill has no bearing on this decision,
   since both mechanisms are fully interchangeable regardless of whether content comes
   from a live system or a static package.

