guarantees; C dismisses a real compliance obligation; D substitutes an unrelated
context-window change for actual content-policy enforcement.)*

**Q7.4 — B.** A hook enforcing path-based restrictions deterministically blocks access
to genuinely sensitive locations, independent of whether the model's own judgment
holds under every circumstance. *(A overstates instruction reliability; C removes
needed files instead of restricting access to them; D misattributes the fix to an
unrelated sampling parameter.)*

**Q7.5 — B.** Standing, periodic rotation limits the exposure window of a credential
that may be compromised without anyone having detected it yet — reactive-only
rotation misses exactly that case. *(A treats reactive rotation as sufficient on its
own; C proposes an impractical extreme; D wrongly claims storage location alone
