**Q8.6 — B.** Bundling matched, always-used-together components into one
distributable plugin is exactly the coordination problem plugins solve, versus manual
per-developer assembly of the same three pieces. *(A treats redundant manual assembly
as a feature rather than friction; C overreaches `CLAUDE.md`'s actual role; D treats
documentation as equivalent to an actual one-step installable package.)*

**Q8.7 — B.** Live external data fits a resource; static, self-contained
procedural/reference knowledge fits a Skill — the source of the content, not its
perceived importance, is what determines the right mechanism. *(A and C each force one
mechanism onto both cases regardless of whether the content actually comes from a live
external system; D denies a real, consequential distinction between the two.)*
